cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this formalization, please cite it as below."
title: "Uniform small-force expansion for reversible diffusions in a random environment: Lean formalization"
type: software
repository-code: "https://github.com/nitromannitol/@REPO@"
abstract: >-
  A Lean 4 and Mathlib formalization of the paper "Uniform small-force expansion for reversible
  diffusions in a random environment" by Ahmed Bou-Rabee and Ruizhe Xu. All twenty-one numbered
  results of the paper are stated and proved for every environment law satisfying Assumptions 1.1
  and 1.2, among them the uniform small-force expansion of the velocity through the critical order
  (Theorem 1.1), the quantitative Einstein relation (Theorem 1.2) and its optimality
  (Proposition 7.1). The proofs use results from the literature, stated in Lean as named axioms with
  their sources; the library contains no sorry. Theorems 1.1 and 1.2 and Proposition 7.1 each have
  a Mathlib-only comparator challenge.
authors:
  - family-names: Bou-Rabee
    given-names: Ahmed
  - family-names: Xu
    given-names: Ruizhe
keywords:
  - Lean
  - mathlib
  - formal verification
  - Einstein relation
  - random environment
  - stochastic homogenization
license: Apache-2.0
